; A forward `br` one byte from its target.
;
; `jr` reaches it with room to spare, and this description emits `jp`: three
; bytes where two would do. The walk that fixes the size has not met `done`
; yet, and guessing short and being wrong emits a jump to somewhere else.
;
; This is the small half of the divergence. `chain.z80` is the half that says
; why a second walk is not the answer either.
        br done
        nop
done:   halt
